    "evidence_text": "Mutation-induced loss of pathway proteins causes downstream proteins to mislocalize, revealing their order of action.\n\nPol IVa acts first, and its localization is RNA dependent, suggesting an RNA template.\n\nThe VTI family of SNARE proteins is necessary for plant viability and mediates different protein transport pathways.\n\nOnly VTI11 and VTI12 are expressed at appreciable levels.\n\nVTI11 was identified recently as the mutated gene in the shoot gravitropic mutant zig.\n\nCoupled local translation and degradation regulate growth cone collapse\n\nThe reason why only specific proteins are locally synthesized is unknown.\n\nPolar PIN localization determines the direction of intercellular auxin flow, yet the mechanisms generating PIN polarity remain unclear.\n\nHere we identify an endocytosis-dependent mechanism of PIN polarity generation and analyse its developmental implications.\n\nThe N-end rule pathway regulates pathogen responses in plants.\n\nMoreover, these abnormalities cannot be recovered by exogenous phytohormones.\n\nLocal, Efflux-Dependent Auxin Gradients as a Common Module for Plant Organ Formation\n\nA molecular framework for plant regeneration.\n\nHere we investigate a local regeneration response in Arabidopsis roots.\n\nThe importance of Rab17 phosphorylation in vivo was assessed in transgenic plants.",
